    <div class="row">
        <div class="span12">
            <h3 class="headline">
                <span>answerOnNextPrompt (text) - Selenium IDE command</span>
            </h3>
        </div> 

        <div class="span12">

            <p> <span class="hired">answerOnNextPrompt</span> tells the IDE what to answer at the next prompt dialog. You find
            an example of such a dialog on this <a href="https://ui.vision/demo/storeeval">test page</a>.</p>
                
             <p>For simple confirmation dialogs (= OK/Cancel dialogs), 
            <a href="/rpa/docs/selenium-ide/assertalert-assertconfirmation-assertprompt#chooseOkOnNextConfirmation">chooseOkOnNextConfirmation</a> was used in the old
            Selenium IDE. It is no longer needed in Kantu, as this behavior is now built-in (<em>Ui.Vision RPA</em> clicks OK automatically).</p>   

                <h3>answerOnNextPrompt Example</h3>
            <p>
                The macro below first opens a prompt, and then <em>Ui.Vision RPA</em> IDE enters "Hello World" in it and closes it automatically.
            </p>

            <p>
                <table class="table table-bordered">
                    <thead>
                    <th class="col-md-2">Command</th>
                    <th class="col-md-5">Target</th>
                    <th class="col-md-5">Pattern/Text</th>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>

                        <tr>
                            <td>open</td>
                            <td>https://ui.vision/demo/javascript </td>
                            <td></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="success">
                            <td>answerOnNextPrompt</td>
                            <td>Hello World!</td>
                            <td>-</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>click</td>
                            <td>//*[@@id="content"]/div[2]/div/p[2]/button[2]</td>
                            <td>-</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </p>

